          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/bloom-filter.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: Bloom Filter\\ndescription: A probabilistic set-membership data structure that uses a bit array and hash functions to answer membership queries with tunable false-positive rates.\\ntimestamp: 2026-01-05T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/DataStructures\\n  - concept/Probabilistic-Algorithms\\n  - pattern/Space-Efficient\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source providing clear definition; widely known computer science concept but this page relies on one source for specific framing.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\nA bloom filter is a probabilistic set-membership structure: it answers \\u0022definitely not present\\u0022 with certainty and \\u0022possibly present\\u0022 with a tunable false-positive rate, using a bit array and k independent hash functions.\\n\\n## Key Characteristics\\n\\n**Certainty and Uncertainty:**\\n- Membership queries return either \\u0022definitely not in the set\\u0022 (with absolute certainty) or \\u0022possibly in the set\\u0022 (with a configurable false-positive probability)\\n- The false-positive rate is tunable: larger bit arrays and more hash functions reduce false positives\\n\\n**Construction:**\\n- Uses a bit array (initialized to all zeros) and k independent hash functions\\n- To insert an element, hash it k times and set the bits at those positions to 1\\n- To test membership, hash the candidate k times and check if all corresponding bits are 1\\n\\n**Limitations:**\\n\\n- **No enumeration:** The filter cannot list or enumerate its members \\u2014 only test for presence\\n- **No deletion:** In its basic form, bloom filters do not support deletion. Removing a set bit could break membership tests for other elements that happen to hash to the same bit positions\\n\\n## Related Concepts\\n\\n- Probabilistic data structures trade accuracy for space and time efficiency\\n- Variants like counting bloom filters and deletable bloom filters address some limitations through different designs\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Bloom filter definition and properties from eval://log-newest-first-placement/sample-05\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
